// TOREADOR — auto-generated lore part (SchreckNET expansion). Hand-authored.
window.LORE_PART_TOREADOR = {
  clans: [
    {
      id: 'toreador',
      name: 'Toreador',
      nickname: 'The Degenerates',
      disciplines: ['Auspex', 'Celerity', 'Presence'],
      weakness: 'The Toreador are enslaved by beauty: confronted with a work of art or a vista of true aesthetic power, they must stop and drink it in, losing minutes or hours to fascination they cannot control.',
      lore_md: [
        'The Clan of the Rose claims to be the keepers of civilization itself. Where the Ventrue build institutions and the Tremere hoard secrets, the Toreador hoard the feeling of being alive — art, fashion, celebrity, scandal, the pulse of a city that never sleeps. Arikel, their founder, was said to be a painter in the First City, and every Toreador still paints with vitae the way the ancients painted with ochre and blood.',
        'They ran the salons of Paris, the opera houses of Vienna, the studios of Hollywood and Milan. Their elders sit on more Camarilla primogen councils than any other clan, because Toreador understand something the others forget: the Camarilla is a performance, and performances need patrons. Their weakness is not vanity — it is hunger. Frozen by true beauty, entranced by a masterpiece or a massacre staged with perfect taste, they have been staked mid-fascination more than once.',
        'The Second Inquisition gutted them like everyone else, but the Toreador adapted fastest: aesthetics became camouflage. Nightclubs, fashion houses, film festivals and streaming fame are all honey traps now. SchreckNET analysts rate the clan as the Camarilla\'s best early-warning system for SI surveillance — Toreador hear a pop song change and know the Technocracy, the SI, or a rival elder is re-staging the city.',
        'The Degenerates despise being called that. They prefer "Artisans of the Night." The epithet was coined by a Ventrue who died soon after, elegantly.'
      ].join('\n\n'),
      chars: [
        { id: 'toreador01', name: 'Arikel', alias: 'THE FIRST PAINTER', gen: '3rd', era: 'First City (mythic)', location: { city: 'Unknown', place: 'torpor, location unrecorded' }, threat: 'high', lore_md: 'The founder of the clan, a painter of the First City whose frescoes are said to have outlived the city itself. Arikel has not been reliably seen since the fall of the Second City, and SchreckNET treats every "new masterpiece in the old style" as a possible signal of his stirring. Rumor: he paints prophecy, and the last canvas was black. Attribution: canonical founder; details are registry apocrypha.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador01.png' },
        { id: 'toreador02', name: 'Helena of Troy', alias: 'THE FACE', gen: '4th', era: 'Bronze Age to present', location: { city: 'Chicago', place: 'torpor beneath the Lakeshore' }, threat: 'high', lore_md: 'The face that launched a thousand ships has been sleeping under Chicago for a century, and the city elders have quietly made her coffin\'s location the third most-guarded secret after the harbor tunnels and the sheriff\'s home address. Even in torpor her blood whispers: two princes have staged wars for the right to be her herald when she wakes. Beware: she is Toreador only by registry claim — some genealogies file her under a different clan entirely.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador02.png' },
        { id: 'toreador03', name: 'Victoria Ash', alias: 'THE HEADLINE', gen: '7th', era: '1970s to present', location: { city: 'Miami', place: 'South Beach fashion circuit' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'The Camarilla\'s leading lady and the clan\'s answer to the Second Inquisition: Victoria Ash does not hide from cameras, she weaponizes them. A famous face is an alibi — nobody believes the person on the magazine cover is the thing in the alley. She has been seen at fundraisers with people the SI would very much like to interview. SchreckNET flag: her entourage includes at least one known blankbody analyst.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador03.png' },
        { id: 'toreador04', name: 'Annabelle Triabell', alias: 'THE MIRROR', gen: '8th', era: '1970s to present', location: { city: 'Los Angeles', place: 'silver-lake gallery circuit' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'A study in self-portraiture: Annabelle made her name exhibiting "documentary" photography of scenes she had personally staged — and some of those scenes included the Final Death of rivals. She treats the Anarch Free States as an art movement with fangs. SchreckNET considers her gallery aCam rally listening post; the parking structure has more cameras than the gallery.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador04.png' },
        { id: 'toreador05', name: 'Marcel Guilbeau', alias: 'THE CANVAS', gen: '6th', era: '1700s to present', location: { city: 'New Orleans', place: 'garden-district salon' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'The old South\'s aesthete-tyrant. Marcel collects portraits — including a rumored portrait of his own sire painted before the Embrace — and lends them out like favors. His salon survives hurricanes, occupation and the SI by the simple method of being boring to everyone but artists. SchreckNET assessment: a safehouse network disguised as an arts endowment.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador05.png' },
        { id: 'toreador06', name: 'Vitae Astra', alias: 'THE PATRON', gen: '8th', era: '1920s to present', location: { city: 'Milan', place: 'quadrilatero fashion district' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'Nobody has ever seen Vitae Astra\'s work, because her art is other people\'s careers. Designers, directors, one pop-star who keeps selling out arenas after dying his first death in a hotel bathtub. She funds museums as mortar for her power base. Milan\'s mortal fashion press knows her as "the silent partner" — the SI knows her as a recurring burner-phone number.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador06.png' },
        { id: 'toreador07', name: 'Rafael de Corazon', alias: 'THE ROSE', gen: '7th', era: '1500s to present', location: { city: 'Barcelona', place: 'gothic quarter residence' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'An elder of the old empire who still speaks of the Camarilla as a young upstart movement, which by his arithmetic it is. Rafael survived the first Inquisition and considers the second one amateur work. His Barcelona townhouse hides a wine cellar with a second, deeper wine cellar. SchreckNET note: he has personally executed two kindred for "aesthetic crimes." Both bodies remain elegant.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador07.png' },
        { id: 'toreador08', name: 'Elaine Fleming', alias: 'THE CURATOR', gen: '9th', era: '1980s to present', location: { city: 'New York', place: 'Chelsea gallery district' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'A young star of the clan who runs an actual, mortal, tax-paying gallery as her power base — and uses openings the way other kindred use Elysium. Elaine trades in exposure the way brokers trade in futures. SchreckNET flagged her guest lists twice: two attendees later vanished into SI holding, one of them an undercover blankbody hunter.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador08.png' },
        { id: 'toreador09', name: 'Dmitri Kovalenko', alias: 'THE DIRECTOR', gen: '9th', era: '1990s to present', location: { city: 'Prague', place: 'barrandov film studios' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'Directs films nobody remembers and trains people nobody forgets: half the Camarilla\'s "performance under surveillance" doctrine was drilled in his soundstages. Prague\'s Hounds trained with him. SchreckNET treats his studio as a clan academy and his cast lists as organizational charts.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador09.png' },
        { id: 'toreador10', name: 'Cecily Bain', alias: 'THE ANARCH ROSE', gen: '10th', era: '2000s to present', location: { city: 'Los Angeles', place: 'koreatown rooftop gardens' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'A Toreador anarch who is beautiful, vicious and extremely online — proof that the clan\'s instincts survive the fall of the Camarilla brand. Cecily runs influence through curated feeds; her aesthetician\'s eye doubles as counter-surveillance (she notices when a backdrop has changed, and why). Registry attribution: she is sometimes filed under Brujah. The file is wrong, and she is flattered.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador10.png' },
        { id: 'toreador11', name: 'Sofia Marchetti', alias: 'THE SCULPTOR', gen: '8th', era: '1800s to present', location: { city: 'Florence', place: 'oltrarno workshop' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'Works in marble and in mortals. Sofia has quietly mentored three generations of Tuscan kindred, and her workshop keeps a locked gallery of pieces she will not sell at any price — SchreckNET believes they are sculptures of people who owed her. Florentine registry files her as Camarilla; the local anarchs call her neutral. Both are useful to her.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador11.png' },
        { id: 'toreador12', name: 'Ji-woo Han', alias: 'THE MUSE', gen: '10th', era: '2010s to present', location: { city: 'Seoul', place: 'hongdae nightlife district' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'Embraced from a K-pop trainee program, Ji-woo understands fan-culture surveillance better than any elder in the Camarilla: stan accounts map kindred movements by accident. She sells that mapping to SchreckNET-adjacent nodes and spends the proceeds on her own image. Threat rating low is a mistake her elders keep making.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador12.png' },
        { id: 'toreador13', name: 'Yves Saint-Clair', alias: 'THE SEAMSTRESS', gen: '8th', era: '1900s to present', location: { city: 'Paris', place: 'marais atelier' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'Dressed three French presidents and two Grand Masters of the Tremere. Yves reads power through cloth: what the court wears reveals what the court fears. After the Vienna chantry burned in 2008, every Tremere survivor passed through his fitting room. SchreckNET flagged his fabric supplier — the invoices list a dye no mortal mill produces.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador13.png' },
        { id: 'toreador14', name: 'Isabel Cortez', alias: 'THE FLAMENCO', gen: '9th', era: '1930s to present', location: { city: 'Seville', place: 'triana tablao' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'Dances three nights a week in a tablao that has burned down twice and never lost its license. Isabel\'s duende is literal: mortals who watch her perform wake with bruised throats and missing evenings. She polices Seville\'s Elysium with a duena\'s fury and has never needed the sheriff. Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent).', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador14.png' },
        { id: 'toreador15', name: 'Osric Fenwick', alias: 'THE CRITIC', gen: '8th', era: 'Victorian to present', location: { city: 'London', place: 'west end private boxes' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'London fell to the Second Inquisition, but Osric kept his seats — the opera house never checks the box holder, only the tuxedo. He survived by becoming the most boring kind of famous: a name on a plaque. Osric\'s reviews of elder "performances" have started fights and ended careers. SchreckNET credits him with warning three princes about SI raids via single-word reviews.', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador15.png' },
        { id: 'toreador16', name: 'Lucia Vasquez', alias: 'THE GRAFFITI QUEEN', gen: '10th', era: '1990s to present', location: { city: 'Buenos Aires', place: 'la boca painted alleys' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'Spray-can cartography: Lucia tags the city\'s shadows to track kindred traffic the way airlines track flights. Her murals are signals only other degenerates can read — and now one more node can, because she trades copies to SchreckNET in exchange for being left alone. Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent).', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador16.png' },
        { id: 'toreador17', name: 'Aurelien Dubois', alias: 'THE SOMMELIER', gen: '9th', era: '1960s to present', location: { city: 'Lyon', place: 'vieux lyon cave restaurant' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'Turned the clan\'s obsession with taste literal: Aurelien catalogs vitae the way mortals catalog vintages, and his cellar book is a blood-line registry the Camarilla would kill to own (it lists generations by flavor). He has been robbed twice. Both thieves were drained and labeled. Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent).', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador17.png' },
        { id: 'toreador18', name: 'Mei Lin Chow', alias: 'THE INK', gen: '10th', era: '2000s to present', location: { city: 'Hong Kong', place: 'central tattoo studios' }, threat: 'low', lore_md: 'A calligrapher-tattooist whose sigils carry Presence: triads pay her to mark them, and marked flesh stays loyal. Hong Kong\'s kindred politics run through her appointment book. SchreckNET interest: her ink formula includes vitae-based fixative stable under UV — a counter-surveillance art form. Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent).', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador18.png' },
        { id: 'toreador19', name: 'Bianca Moretti', alias: 'THE DIVA', gen: '8th', era: '1930s to present', location: { city: 'Verona', place: 'arena opera boxes' }, threat: 'mid', lore_md: 'An opera singer who faked her own mortal death in 1951 and now attends her own anniversary performances in disguise. Bianca\'s voice carries Majesty even unassisted, and Verona\'s court survives because she finds blood feuds gauche. She has been campaigning for decades to have the Toreador rename themselves "Artisans." It will fail. She will keep trying. Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent).', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador19.png' },
        { id: 'toreador20', name: 'The Patron of Glass', alias: 'UNNAMED', gen: 'unknown', era: 'unknown', location: { city: 'Dubai', place: 'unknown' }, threat: 'high', lore_md: 'A recurring figure in SI debriefs: an unnamed benefactor who buys entire glass skyscrapers through shell funds and then commissions one artwork per building — all depicting drowning. No name, no registry entry, no confirmed face. SchreckNET links the pattern to pre-Gehenna prophecy-mongering. Treat as a methuselah\'s art consultant until proven otherwise. Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent).', photo: 'assets/img/char_toreador20.png' }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
